    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Junior Caminero** serving as the undisputed engine of the lineup, boasting an elite score of 81.92. His high marks are anchored by a favorable park factor and a matchup against Baz that provides the best environmental synergy on the board. We also see significant value in the top-of-the-order aggression from **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (66.51), whose score is inflated by a \"green light\" scenario against a pitcher with a slow delivery, maximizing his stolen base potential\u2014our highest priority category. Meanwhile, **Christian Encarnacion-Strand** (65.61) is a primary start today; despite the neutral platoon, his ability to capitalize on the 4.70 xERA of Martinez, N creates an ideal threshold for power production.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision involved the marginal 40.11 score of **Chase Meidroth**. While his projection is bolstered by favorable wind conditions, he represents the floor of our current active roster. **Colt Keith** was the closest contender for a spot; however, his platoon disadvantage against a left-handed starter effectively neutralized his raw projection, leading us to favor the offensive environment surrounding **Meidroth**. We remain cautious regarding **Yordan Alvarez** (53.21); while his elite 0.459 xwOBA is undeniable, the combination of a lefty-lefty platoon disadvantage and a modest 3.64 xERA matchup results in a lower-than-usual confidence score. We are keeping a close eye on **Casey Schmitt**, who remains sidelined on the IL, alongside our other bench depth like **Dillon Dingler**, **Josh Smith**, **Jacob Gonzalez**, **Hector Rodriguez**, **Luis Pena**, and **Pedro Ramirez**, none of whom were required to fill gaps today given the current health of our active starters.",
